  "id": "m3b-form-diagnostics-lowered-compact-exponent",
  "description": "The same catalog as m3b-form-diagnostics-sparse with maximumCompactExponent lowered to 3, so a PluralOperands record carrying compactExponent 10 -- perfectly legal at PluralOperands' own default ceiling of 64 -- is refused by the INSTANCE limit inside DefaultStrings.ordinalityForValue's validatePluralOperands call rather than at operand construction. Separating the two ceilings is the whole point of the fixture.",
